RATIONALE: Three unrebutted REDs on independent, substantive grounds; prior-art search was inadequate. The claim's stated novelty has three load-bearing pillars, and all three are broken:

(1) MECHANISM NOVELTY ("chunk granularity degrades streaming moderation recall via boundary-straddling phrases") — COLLAPSED. NeMo Guardrails' streaming output-rail configuration explicitly parameterizes chunk_size (tokens buffered before the output rail runs) and context_size (overlap tokens carried across chunk boundaries), with documentation stating context_size gives rails visibility across chunk boundaries. The code (RollingBuffer) implements exactly the sliding-window-with-overlap moderator the L0 tests. Two reviewers independently cite this with specific URLs and parameter names, meeting the >=2-source collision bar. The mechanism is not merely known as folklore — it is shipped, documented, and parameterized in the dominant production framework.

(2) RECOVERY LAW ("W* ≈ 2C is a novel finding") — COLLAPSED. W >= C + L_max - 1 is the textbook overlap condition for any windowed scanner over chunked input (cf. HF token-classification stride, RAG chunk-overlap, streaming-ASR windowing). The theory_skeptic correctly identifies the L0 result as a controlled re-measurement of this known invariant. No goodness-of-fit test against the predicted law was performed — if the fit is exact, the result IS the known invariant.

(3) ORG-SEAM NOVELTY ("runtime team sets chunk_size without knowing safety team's max-phrase-length — first uncrossed cross-area seam") — UNSUPPORTED. This is the only potential residual novelty, and it has zero evidence. No config survey, no postmortem, no team-structure citation. The dominant production pattern (NeMo) co-locates chunk_size and context_size in a single config, closing the seam by construction. The claim assumes separate ownership but does not demonstrate it.

Additionally, the evaluation_prosecutor's strawman concern is damning: W=16 (≈12 words of context) is implausibly small for any production safety filter that performs semantic moderation. Llama-Guard-class models require 128+ tokens of context. At realistic W, the condition W >= 2*C is trivially satisfied for all tested C, and the fragmentation effect is zero. The packet provides no latency/memory justification for why W would ever be this small.

The L0 execution quality is genuinely high — prereg before run, anti-circular design, sanity ceiling, null controls, honest reporting. The theory_skeptic and product_realist rightly credit this. But execution quality cannot rescue a claim whose mechanism is prior-implemented and whose novelty premise (the uncrossed seam) is both undemonstrated and contradicted by the production landscape. The finding reduces to: "we re-measured a known chunk-overlap effect in a toy harness with an unrealistically small window and called it novel because we didn't check NeMo Guardrails."

